<p class="lede">This notice explains how we process your personal data when you use the Booster Auth website and license portal. It applies to
    portal users, trial applicants, authorised and contact persons of customer companies, people who contact support and site visitors.</p>
<div class="callout"><p>This notice is for information only; it does not require your consent. None of the processing below relies on explicit consent.
    When you run the Booster Auth software on your own servers, the data controller for end-user data processed in it is the organisation running the
    software, not us; the software sends no data to us.</p></div>

<h2 id="controller">Data controller</h2>
<p><b>@Legal.CompanyName</b>, @Legal.Address · MERSIS: @Legal.Mersis · KEP: @Legal.Kep · E-mail: @Legal.KvkkEmail</p>

<h2 id="processing">What we process, why and on which legal basis</h2>
<div class="table-scroll">
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Activity</th><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis (KVKK art.5/2)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>Portal account and sign-in</td>
            <td>Name, e-mail, whether the e-mail is verified, user ID; session cookies during sign-in</td>
            <td>Secure sign-in to the portal, linking actions to the right company</td>
            <td>(c) conclusion and performance of a contract</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sign-in service account</td>
            <td>In our Booster Auth sign-in service: e-mail, password hash, two-factor data, session and sign-in records, IP address, browser details</td>
            <td>Account creation, authentication, account security and abuse prevention</td>
            <td>(c) performance of a contract; (f) legitimate interest for security logs</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Company and billing details</td>
            <td>Legal name, billing e-mail, tax office and number, address (may be personal data for sole proprietors)</td>
            <td>Orders, invoicing, issuing the license in the company's name</td>
            <td>(c) performance of a contract; (ç) legal obligation (tax and commercial law) for invoicing and retention</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Installation records</td>
            <td>Installation ID (GUID), installation name, domains</td>
            <td>Binding the license to the right installation and domains, transfers</td>
            <td>(c) performance of a contract</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Trial license requests</td>
            <td>E-mail and domain, IP address, time of request, result, accepted agreement version</td>
            <td>Applying the trial rules (company e-mail, one trial per domain, daily limit per IP), preventing abuse, proving acceptance of the agreement</td>
            <td>(c) conclusion of a contract; (f) legitimate interest for abuse prevention and evidence</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Orders and payment</td>
            <td>Order details, e-mail of the ordering user, time and IP address of acceptance of the terms, bank transfer record (sender name, amount, description)</td>
            <td>Receiving the order, matching the payment, generating the license, proving acceptance of the contract</td>
            <td>(c) performance of a contract; (ç) legal obligation; (e) establishing and protecting a right, for evidence</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Licenses and transfers</td>
            <td>Company name written into the license, installation ID, domains, limits; e-mail of the user requesting a transfer</td>
            <td>Generating, re-displaying and transferring licenses</td>
            <td>(c) performance of a contract</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Transactional e-mails</td>
            <td>Billing e-mail address, company name, order and license details</td>
            <td>Trial license, order confirmation, license delivery, transfer notice and renewal reminders</td>
            <td>(c) performance of a contract</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Support requests</td>
            <td>Name, e-mail, phone, content of the request, attachments you share</td>
            <td>Answering and resolving the request</td>
            <td>(c) performance of a contract; (f) legitimate interest</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Site and portal logs</td>
            <td>IP address, requested address, date and time, browser details</td>
            <td>Operating the site, troubleshooting and security</td>
            <td>(f) legitimate interest</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Disputes</td>
            <td>The relevant records above</td>
            <td>Pursuing and defending legal claims</td>
            <td>(e) establishing, exercising or protecting a right</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>We do not send marketing e-mails. If we want to in the future, we will ask for a separate, optional consent; not giving it will not affect any service.</p>

<h2 id="collection">How we collect data</h2>
<p>From the forms you fill in in the portal; from the identity data our sign-in service passes to the portal (name, e-mail, user ID); from records and
    cookies created automatically when you use the site and portal; from bank transfer records at our bank; and from the e-mails and phone calls you send
    to support. If your company names another employee as billing or contact person, we provide this notice to that person at the first contact.</p>

<h2 id="recipients">Who receives the data</h2>
<ul>
    <li><b>Hosting and network providers:</b> the infrastructure running the site and portal (@Legal.HostingEn) and the network / tunnel service the traffic
        passes through (Cloudflare). They process data only to provide the service.</li>
    <li><b>E-mail provider:</b> for sending transactional e-mails (@Legal.SmtpProviderEn).</li>
    <li><b>Support system provider:</b> for support e-mails (@Legal.HelpdeskProviderEn).</li>
    <li><b>Banks, our accountant and e-invoice integrator:</b> for payments and invoicing.</li>
    <li><b>Competent public authorities and courts:</b> where required by law.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="transfers">International transfers</h2>
<p>Because the network / tunnel service (Cloudflare) is located abroad, your IP address and request details are
    transferred abroad when this service is used.
    [If the hosting or e-mail provider is abroad, state the country and the KVKK art.9 mechanism here, e.g. "The standard contract published by the
    Personal Data Protection Board has been signed and notified to the Authority." If they are in Turkey and Cloudflare is not used,
    replace this section with "Your personal data is not transferred abroad." Continuous transfers cannot rely on explicit consent.]</p>

<h2 id="retention">How long we keep data</h2>
<div class="table-scroll">
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Period</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>Invoices, orders, contracts and acceptance records</td><td>10 years (TTK art.82)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Customer account, company, installation and license records</td><td>Term of the contract and 10 years after it ends</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Trial requests that did not lead to a purchase</td><td>12 months after the trial ends</td></tr>
        <tr><td>IP addresses in trial requests (abuse limit)</td><td>90 days</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Security and session records</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Support requests</td><td>2 years after closure; shared logs and screenshots @Legal.SupportLogDeleteDays days after closure</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>When the period ends, data is deleted, destroyed or anonymised.</p>

<h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
<p>Under KVKK art.11 you may apply to us to:</p>
<ul>
    <li>learn whether your personal data is processed and, if so, request information about it;</li>
    <li>learn the purpose of processing and whether the data is used in line with it;</li>
    <li>know the third parties in Turkey or abroad to whom your data is transferred;</li>
    <li>ask for incomplete or inaccurate data to be corrected, and for data to be erased or destroyed where the grounds for processing no longer exist, and
        for these actions to be notified to recipients;</li>
    <li>object to a result against you arising solely from automated analysis;</li>
    <li>claim compensation if you suffer damage from unlawful processing.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="requests">How to apply</h2>
<ul>
    <li>By a signed letter: @Legal.Address</li>
    <li>By KEP: @Legal.Kep</li>
    <li>By e-mail signed with a secure electronic or mobile signature: @Legal.KvkkEmail</li>
    <li>From the e-mail address you previously gave us and that is registered in our systems: @Legal.KvkkEmail</li>
</ul>
<p>Please state your name, signature (for written applications), Turkish ID number (for foreigners, nationality and passport number), address for
    notifications, e-mail and phone if any, and your request. We will conclude your application free of charge within <b>30 days</b> at the latest; if it
    involves additional cost, a fee may be charged according to the Board's tariff. If your application is rejected, you find the answer insufficient or we
    do not answer in time, you may complain to the Personal Data Protection Board.</p>

<h2 id="security">Security</h2>
<p>Portal traffic is encrypted in transit; sign-in requires accounts with verified e-mail addresses; access rights are restricted; and the license signing
    key is stored encrypted. In case of a data breach we notify the Board and the affected people within the time required by law.</p>

<h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
<p>Only strictly necessary cookies are used on the site and portal. Details are in the <a href="/en/legal/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>

<h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
<p>We update this notice before processing data for a new purpose. The current version and its date are published on this page. The Turkish text is
    binding; this translation is provided for information.</p>
